<title>SINGAPORE: UPP 1996 net profit up five percent.</title>
<headline>UPP 1996 net profit up five percent.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				2.14 vs   2.04</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)		    5.00 vs   4.00</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (cents)	  1.86 vs   1.79</p>
<p>    Turnover				 67.31 vs  68.32</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		    1.83 vs   2.23</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortization	   5.98 vs   5.66</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			  3.58 vs   1.72</p>
<p>    Tax					 1.44 vs   0.32</p>
<p>    Extraordinary loss		    0.15 vs   nil</p>
<p>Note - United Pulp and Paper is a timber company.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
